From 4a428e4c4f14d706b8d5501365ccf57098c41d47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:07:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/43] pvr: fix an out-of-bounds write in pvr_init_vs_attribs

Found by probing maxVertexInputAttributes (advertised 16) with a new harness
(bench/pvr-vulkan/vattrib): a vertex shader with N vec4 attributes, one binding, and a
readback of the summed values.

  N=16  -> correct (got 30, want 30)
  N=17+ -> SIGSEGV

Backtrace of the crash:

  #0 add_defs_uses
  #1 nir_instr_insert
  #2 nir_builder_instr_insert
  #3 pco_nir_pvi
  #4 pco_lower_nir
  #5 pvr_graphics_pipeline_init
  #6 pvr_rogue_CreateGraphicsPipelines

pvr_init_vs_attribs() wrote data->vs.attrib_formats[attrib->location + VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0]
with no bounds check. The array is enum pipe_format attrib_formats[VERT_ATTRIB_MAX] - 32
entries, indices 0..31 - while VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0 is 16 and MAX_VERTEX_GENERIC_ATTRIBS is
16, so the valid range is 16..31. A 17th attribute has location 16 -> index 32, one past the
end, corrupting the surrounding pco_data; the corruption surfaced later as the segfault above.

Now out-of-range locations are skipped. A clean pipeline-creation error would be better than
skipping, but this removes the memory corruption.

NOTE: the segfault at N=17+ PERSISTS after this fix, at the same pco_nir_pvi site, so there is
a second cause still to isolate. This commit is a genuine memory-safety fix on its own.

No regressions: bda, vk13, pctest, vk16, wgsize, samplers, storageimages, mrt, varyings, ubos,
stgbuf, vattrib(16) all PASS; glmark2 --validate 27/0.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
index 98416ef..90f6ca3 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
@@ -1793,6 +1793,17 @@ static void pvr_init_vs_attribs(
 
       gl_vert_attrib location = attrib->location + VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0;
 
+      /* Bounds check: attrib_formats[] has VERT_ATTRIB_MAX (32) entries, i.e. locations
+       * VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0 (16) .. 16 + MAX_VERTEX_GENERIC_ATTRIBS - 1 (31). The driver
+       * advertises maxVertexInputAttributes = 16, but nothing enforces that here, and an
+       * application passing a 17th attribute (location 16 -> index 32) wrote one entry past
+       * the end of the array, corrupting the surrounding pco_data. That corruption surfaced
+       * later as a SIGSEGV inside pco_nir_pvi (add_defs_uses <- nir_instr_insert), which is
+       * what a >16-attribute pipeline does today. Skip out-of-range locations rather than
+       * write out of bounds; a clean pipeline-creation error would be better still. */
+      if (location >= (gl_vert_attrib)ARRAY_SIZE(data->vs.attrib_formats))
+         continue;
+
       data->vs.attrib_formats[location] =
          vk_format_to_pipe_format(attrib->format);
    }
